  // ------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Issue #67 — IO / import-export / pixel-format surface
  // (AE_IO.h, PR_Public.h, PT_Public.h, FIEL_Public.h,
  // AE_IO_ColorMetadata.h, AE_IO_FileExt.h, AE_BlendModes.h,
  // AE_EffectPixelFormat.h, SDK 26.5). AEIO_* are plug-in-
  // implemented entry points the host calls (in-host-plugin-
  // command); PR_*/PT_*Func are artisan/tracker entry-point
  // typedefs. The IO entry-point table's only declaration is the
  // versioned struct `AEIO_FunctionBlock4` (AE_IO.h); `member`
  // names the `AEIO_*` proc declared inside it. Three registered
  // callbacks are NOT block members: AEIO_MessageFunc is the
  // `msg_func` field type of the in-data struct (AEIO_BasicData)
  // and AEIO_AbortProc/AEIO_ProgressProc are the `abort0`/
  // `progress0` field types of AEIO_InterruptFuncs — `suite`
  // names those declaring structs and `member` the proc typedef
  // (Issue #215). File-writing entries declare write semantics and
  // are individually gated — never retried on unknown (FR-07/FR-12
  // disposable-project fixtures; real-host evidence requires an
  // owned AE session). FIEL/BlendModes/PixelFormat headers carry
  // data types only — no callable surface to register.
